# Every .txt in this repository is a signed plugin / indicator / strategy
# payload, and every .sig beside it is an Ed25519 signature over the RAW
# BYTES of that file.
#
# Git's default end-of-line handling silently breaks that. With
# core.autocrlf=true — the DEFAULT on Windows — checkout rewrites every LF
# to CRLF, so the bytes on disk are no longer the bytes that were signed and
# every signature fails to verify. Measured 2026-08-05: a stock Windows
# clone made OpenTrader-Pro's install_from_path reject all 33 payloads as
# `invalid_signature` and install NOTHING, i.e. the marketplace was entirely
# unusable on Windows, with no error that pointed at line endings.
#
# `-text` (rather than `binary`, which is `-text -diff`) disables EOL
# conversion in both directions while keeping diffs readable in review.
#
# The committed blobs are already LF, so this changes no content and needs
# NO re-signing — it only stops checkout from corrupting what is already
# correct in the object store.
* -text
